body: "Source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1457\n\n## Problem (2026.10.13, also 2026.10.10)\nWhen `pm list` output is truncated by the default output token budget, the response carries `next_cursor`, but that cursor is an **output cursor** (`continuation_kind: \"output_cursor\"`). An agent following the help text cannot use it:\n- `pm list --help` documents `--after <cursor>` as \"Continue after an opaque next_cursor from a previous list response\".\n- `pm list --help` does **not** list `--output-cursor` at all.\n- `pm list … --after <that next_cursor>` refuses with `invalid_query_cursor` / \"Query cursor version or payload is unsupported\". The refusal has no recovery hint and never mentions `--output-cursor`, even though the same cursor works with `--output-cursor`.\n\nThe only pointer is buried in `output_budget_truncation.recovery.cli = \"--output-cursor\"`.\n\n## Reproduction (synthetic, about 1 minute)\n```sh\nT=$(mktemp -d) && cd \"$T\" && git init -q && export PM_PATH=$T/.agents/pm PM_AUTHOR=repro\npm init --prefix cr\nfor i in $(seq 1 120); do pm create --type Task --title \"Synthetic continuation item number $i with a deliberately long title\" --description \"$(printf 'padding %.0s' $(seq 1 40))\"; done\nc=$(pm --json list --status all --limit 500 | jq -r .next_cursor)   # applied_limit 33, truncated, continuation_kind output_cursor\npm --json list --status all --limit 500 --after \"$c\"               # invalid_query_cursor, no recovery command\npm --json list --status all --limit 500 --output-cursor \"$c\"       # works (next 33 rows)\n```\n\n## Real-world impact\nA script mirroring 266 knowledge items wrote the documented loop (`--limit 500`, then follow `next_cursor` with `--after`). It failed on the second page. An earlier version that took `.items` without checking `truncated` would silently have seen only the first 129 of 266 rows (the budget cut `--limit 500` down to 129), and would have created duplicates on re-runs.\n\n## Proposal\n1. `--after` should accept an output cursor for the same query fingerprint and continue transparently, since both are opaque continuation tokens for the same query. If they must stay distinct, refuse with a recovery command that substitutes `--output-cursor <cursor>`.\n2. List `--output-cursor` in `pm list --help` (and in search/context help), and make the `--after` help say which `continuation_kind` it accepts.\n3. Consider naming the field after the flag that consumes it: keep `next_cursor` for query cursors and use `next_output_cursor` for budget continuations, or document that `continuation_kind` decides the flag.\n\nRelated closed work: #1371 (budget continuation across producer cursors).\n\n\nIntake scope\n\nInvestigate and correct reported continuation-kind confusion: budget next_cursor passed to documented --after is rejected without executable --output-cursor recovery, while help hides the consuming flag. Include the same report’s --no-truncate plus explicit --limit behavior.\n\nDuplicate check: complete live2953-item all-status corpus and request-specific search/open/in-progress reads. Full pm-gh1371 is closed for composed pagination and its111-entry history verifies; this report concerns flag discoverability/refusal recovery and no-truncate with explicit limit, not the completed traversal fix. Reuse open pm-f05lsg recovery programme as parent; add related closed pm-gh1371 without reopening shipped work. GH issue body and all paginated comments, including no-truncate follow-up6147611703, read. Reproduction remains pending in this intake."
